{"term":"enforce","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:6adc7d21d0d75c866e","definition":"To keep up, impose or bring into effect something, not necessarily by force.","example":"The police are there to enforce the law.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["enforceability","enforceable","enforcedly","enforcement","enforcer","enforcibility","enforcingly","enforcive","misenforce","nonenforced","nonenforcing","overenforce","re-enforce","reenforce","underenforce","unenforced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8417e5b0a5da0a52cc","definition":"To apply a rule or enforcement action to a person or user account.","example":"This will give us the tools we need to enforce accounts like these.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["enforceability","enforceable","enforcedly","enforcement","enforcer","enforcibility","enforcingly","enforcive","misenforce","nonenforced","nonenforcing","overenforce","re-enforce","reenforce","underenforce","unenforced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6dd9f5a7833c36a7a9","definition":"To give strength or force to; to affirm, to emphasize.","example":"The victim was able to enforce his evidence against the alleged perpetrator.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["enforceability","enforceable","enforcedly","enforcement","enforcer","enforcibility","enforcingly","enforcive","misenforce","nonenforced","nonenforcing","overenforce","re-enforce","reenforce","underenforce","unenforced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contribu