d by Caluin, that any one sentence of Scripture doth necessarily enforce these things, or the rest wherein your opinion concurreth with his against the orders of your owne Church?","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"obsolete","register":"obsolete","wordFamily":["enforceability","enforceable","enforcedly","enforcement","enforcer","enforcibility","enforcingly","enforcive","misenforce","nonenforced","nonenforcing","overenforce","re-enforce","reenforce","underenforce","unenforced"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/enforce#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"}],"pronunciation":{"ipa":"/ɪnˈfoɹs/"},"wordFamily":["enforceability","enforceable","enforcedly","enforcement","enforcer","enforcibility","enforcingly","enforcive","misenforce","nonenforced","nonenforcing","overenforce","re-enforce","reenforce","underenforce","unenforced"]}